# 🚨 BLOCKING — fixed: `postPrComment` now invalidates the memoized ledger read

**Fix** (`js/common/smProvider.js`, GitHub provider `postPrComment`): the write now drops the
per-tick comment memo immediately after `github_create_comment` — the house
invalidate-after-mutation primitive this review cited:

```js
postPrComment: function (prNumber, body) {
    var out = github_create_comment({
        workspace: owner, repository: repo,
        pullRequestId: String(prNumber), text: body
    });
    // Invalidate-after-mutation (gh-1352 review, the gh-957 house primitive)
    ioCacheDrop(owner, repo, 'prVerdicts', String(prNumber));
    return out;
}
```

The failure chain is closed: the next deferral's `prCommentList()` re-fetches, sees the marker
posted by the previous deferral, and appends onto it — the marker family can no longer
last-write-wins over earlier `defered` findings.

**Regression tests (written first, RED before the fix — the final marker held 1 finding, not 2):**

- `js/unit-tests/test_machineSmAgent.js` — *"gh-1352 BLOCKING replay: two deferrals in one tick
  BOTH land in the final ledger marker (memoized provider)"*: the **real** `smProvider` GitHub
  face (memoized `_ghFetchPrComments`, live server list behind mocked `github_*` globals) drives
  `resolveSuggestionThreads` with 2 machine suggestion threads; the test parses the LAST posted
  `dmtools:review-debt-ledger` marker and asserts both findings with both `originThread` ids.
  Exactly the shape the review asked for: the read stream serves the memoized snapshot, ≥2
  deferrals, the final marker must contain both findings.
- `js/unit-tests/test_smProvider.js` — new suite *"gh-1352 ledger primitives"*:
  - the post invalidates the memo (a same-tick re-read re-fetches and observes the post);
  - reads still memoize — the drop rides the WRITE, never the read (no over-invalidation);
  - the memo re-arms after each write (a post-poisoned read never sticks).

Verified: full suite green; `node scripts/dry-run-disposition-loop.js` still `DRY-RUN PASS`.

